    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster, as his elite 81.88 score cements him as the must-start of the day. Facing Warren, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a strong platoon advantage, providing the highest ceiling in the lineup. Close behind, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), **Kyle Tucker** (74.09), and **Jackson Merrill** (73.43) offer immense value; each is bolstered by a potent combination of advantageous matchups against middling SP_xERA arms and their status as primary contributors in Roto categories. **Andy Pages** also represents a sharp play (72.37) against Freeland, with the park and SP skill factors pushing his efficiency well above the baseline.\n\nThe decision to bench **Dominic Smith** (51.37) was the most difficult call of the morning. While his output against Bradley is statistically viable, he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace the high-upside profiles of **Drake Baldwin** or **Coby Mayo**, both of whom project for higher run-scoring potential. We are monitoring **Nasim Nunez** closely; while his 52.03 score is marginal, his elite speed profile remains a critical asset for our league-wide pursuit of stolen bases. Risk remains localized, particularly with **Miguel Vargas**; while he is in the lineup, his score is slightly suppressed by a BvP-adjacent concern regarding a high-hold opposing pitcher who historically discourages stolen base attempts. We remain without the production of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** due to their respective IL or bench designations, leaving our active group to shoulder the burden of maintaining our efficiency in the 5x5 race.",
